From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: do not drop a runtime PM reference that was not
 taken

pm_runtime_resume_and_get() drops the usage count it took when the
resume fails. iris_hfi_queue_cmd_write() nevertheless jumps to its exit
path, which calls pm_runtime_put_sync() once more. With no other
reference held, every command issued while the core fails to resume
logs "Runtime PM usage count underflow!". With another reference held,
for instance by a concurrent command, the extra put drops that one
instead, and the device can runtime suspend under its holder.

Return the error directly when the resume fails.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_queue.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_queue.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_queue.c
index bf6db23b53..545bbe75e1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_queue.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_queue.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ int iris_hfi_queue_cmd_write(struct iris_core *core, void *pkt, u32 pkt_size)
 
 	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(core->dev);
 	if (ret < 0)
-		goto exit;
+		return ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
 	ret = iris_hfi_queue_cmd_write_locked(core, pkt, pkt_size);
